## Getting started

**Cloned this repo?** Run setup first — client integrations are not in git.

```bash
cp .env.example .env          # required — .env is git-ignored
frai setup --claude           # CLI mode: MCPs + slash commands (pick your client)
# frai setup --codex
# frai setup --cursor
frai check
frai exec AnalyzeItem::Task "query(hello world)"
```

**Do not skip `frai setup` after clone.** The repo has `mcp/*.rb`, but `.claude/commands/`, Codex MCP registration, and `.cursor/mcp.json` are created locally by setup. Without it, CLI/HITL mode will not see MCPs or task commands.

| Step | In git? | After clone |
|---|---|---|
| `mcp/*.rb`, tasks, agents | yes | ready |
| `.env` | no | `cp .env.example .env` and fill in |
| `.claude/commands/`, client MCP config | no | `frai setup --claude` / `--codex` / `--cursor` |

**API mode only** (`LLM_MODEL` set): setup is optional. You still need `cp .env.example .env`.

**New task in an existing project:**

```bash
frai gt analyze_item
frai setup --claude           # re-run after adding tasks or MCP servers
frai check
```

This project starts in **dry run** (`FRAI_ENV=development`): scripts run, prompts render, no API key needed. For production, set `FRAI_ENV=production` — leave `LLM_MODEL` empty for CLI mode (prompt only) or set it for API mode.

